{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelSquared","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelSquared","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelLevel"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_one_lt_required","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_one_lt_required","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelSquared.lean#L63-L72","doc":"**Corollary: the level-1 kernel alone is strictly short whenever `n ≥ 1`.**  Its exponent\n`C(n+1,2)` is strictly below the required `n(n+1)`, so no single level-1 division can remove the\ngrowth — the gap is another full copy of the same kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernel_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernel_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelSquared.lean#L56-L61","doc":"**The squared level-1 kernel has exponent `n(n+1)`.**  `t_{n+1}² = q^{n(n+1)}`, the divisor the\nprobe measures as the one that removes `Z_n`'s quadratic growth exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_qBorelExp_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_qBorelExp_one","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelSquared.lean#L50-L54","doc":"**The required divisor is exactly the level-1 exponent doubled.**  `2·qBorelExp 1 (n+1) =\nn(n+1)`.  One application of the level-1 q-Borel kernel supplies half of what `Z_n(q₀)` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_choose_two_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_choose_two_succ","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelSquared.lean#L37-L48","doc":"**Twice the triangular number.**  `2·C(n+1,2) = n(n+1)`.\n\nStated at `n+1` deliberately: `C(n,2) = n(n-1)/2` involves truncated subtraction on `ℕ`, whereas\n`C(n+1,2) = n(n+1)/2` does not, so the doubled form is subtraction-free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}